<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=metric-system">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Writing and counting</p><h1 class="enc-title">Metric system</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1790s</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as decimal system of measurement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The metric system standardises base units and names large and small quantities with decimal prefixes such as kilo and milli. Its first form was devised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the late 18th century: in 1790 Charles Maurice de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-maurice-de-talleyrand">Talleyrand</a> proposed Lavoisier's system based on natural units to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-assembly-of-france">National Assembly</a>, a commission defined the metre in 1791 as one ten-millionth of the distance from the equator to the North Pole, and the system was launched in France in 1799. Gabriel Mouton had proposed a decimal system based on the Earth around 1665–1670. The International System of Units derives from it and is the official system in almost all countries.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Academies, encyclopaedias, museums and scientific societies multiplied, and the <b>metric system</b>, adopted in revolutionary France in the 1790s, was a product of the same wish for rational order.</blockquote><a href="/movement/enlightenment">Enlightenment · Outcomes</a></li><li><blockquote>The decimal <b>metric system</b> has since been adopted almost worldwide.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-1">1 August in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1799</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>France</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/encyclopedia/antoine-lavoisier">Antoine Lavoisier</a> · <a href="/encyclopedia/charles-maurice-de-talleyrand">Charles-Maurice de Talleyrand</a> · Gabriel Mouton</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Around 1665–1670 Gabriel Mouton suggested replacing France's many units with a single decimal system based on a minute of arc of the Earth; his ideas were clearly the basis of the 1790s system, though his contribution is sometimes overlooked.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=metric-system">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
